# Environment Configuration

How development, staging, and production configuration is represented.

## Requirements

- Keep environment-specific values outside feature widgets.
- Must not commit secrets in source, assets, config files, or docs.
- Use Flutter compile-time define files for non-secret public values.
- Validate required configuration during startup and separate per-environment values.
- Production API base URLs must use HTTPS unless a controlled private network requires otherwise.
- Logs must identify the environment without exposing secrets.

## Recommended values

| Value | Example |
|---|---|
| environment name | `development`, `staging`, `production` |
| API base URL | public non-secret URL |
| API timeout | duration in seconds |
| logging level | debug/info/warn/error |
| feature flag defaults | safe defaults |

## Acceptance

- Missing required config fails fast with a clear message.
- Production builds exclude development-only endpoints.
- Tests can override environment config.

